  "Extensions this main opens:" (each extension with its icon),
  "Conflicting extensions:" (each extension another main also claims, naming that main).

Data: see DataReadDataEditDesign.

Logs: the log files the mains wrote in `.out/logs`, with a Logs button opening that folder in the file explorer.

Every entry of `projects.info` about a project except `path` shows in the project area of that project, and every entry except `kind` has a GUI operation that removes that entry.

## Run, Compile and Check

A project runs at most one thing at a time: a compilation, or the mains of one `Run`, one after the other.
A compilation of a project runs from the start of `Coordinator.compile` to the end of the last step of What the manager does after `Coordinator.compile`.
A project is 'in use' while a main or a compilation of the project is currently running, and while a main of a project with a mount of the project is currently running.
Everything a running main or a compilation prints goes to the Output, and the Output marks where each main and the compilation start and end, and how each of them ended.

- A compilation runs in a JVM of its own, and each main runs in a JVM of its own (`Coordinator.run`, see CoordinatorDesign).
- The report of a `Check`, and the changes of a `Fix` (see Fix in FolderShapesDesign), go to the Output; a `Check` and a `Fix` start no JVM, and the Output has no marks for a `Check` or a `Fix`.
- Terminate ends the running main: the JVM of that main ends, and no further main of that `Run` starts.
- A main or a compilation that crashes, or that takes all the memory, ends alone: the manager and the mains and compilations of the other projects keep running.


### Files changing while a main runs
An 'autoCheck' of a project with a running main that finds the project 'invalid' or 'out of date' terminates that main, and writes in the Output of the project the error `Some files inside the project "hello" were updated while main "hello.Hello" was running.`


## File associations

### Invariants and transitions

```
M                  the manager; id(M) its identity; folder(M) its manager folder
D                  the desktop of the system
fearless           the Fearless extensions: .fearless, .fapp000 .. .fapp999, .ffile000 .. .ffile999
reserve(M)         the 'reserve' of M: the list reserve of projects.info (see Registered projects)
cached(M)          the registered projects of M whose .fearless_out holds a <pkg>.json
claims(p)          the extensions of the claims of Coordinator.cachedMains of p
captured(M)        the 'captured extensions' of M: fearless union reserve(M)
setup(D, i)        the extensions the setup of the identity i names on D
holder(D, e)       the program D opens a file x<e> with
family(D)          the identities of the Fearless family with a setup on D
single(D, f)       the OS processes of D that are the 'single' manager of the manager folder f
```

After every `.reconcile` of M that ends with no refusal, once the EditMetadata calling that `.reconcile`, if any, applies, while no other program changes D:
```
I1  setup(D, id(M)) = captured(M)
I2  forall e in captured(M). holder(D, e) = id(M)
I3  forall p in cached(M). claims(p) subset of captured(M)
I4  |family(D)| <= 1
```
At every moment:
```
I5  forall f. |single(D, f)| <= 1
I6  M running && !exists(folder(M)) && M did not delete folder(M)  =>  M is applying Quit, and M changes nothing on D
```

The transitions:
```
T1  a .reconcile of M refuses because a program outside the Fearless family holds an e not in taken:
      the manager asks the user to let the manager hold e: once when e not in fearless, one or more times when e in fearless;
      the user accepts each such e  =>  .reconcile again, with those extensions as taken

T2  the user rejects the last question for e, or .reconcile can not take e:
      e in fearless  =>  'fatal error' naming e
      the user rejects the last question for e, and the EditMetadata of this .reconcile adds e to reserve(M)
                    =>  that EditMetadata is refused, and changes nothing
      otherwise     =>  for each p in cached(M) with e in claims(p): end the mains and the compilation of p,
                        and delete the compilation cache of p (Coordinator.deleteCache);
                        reserve(M) := reserve(M) \ {e};
                        .reconcile again

T3  a compilation of p ends with e in claims(p) \ captured(M):
      reserve(M) := reserve(M) union {e}, and .reconcile

T4  only T2, T3 and an EditMetadata change reserve(M)
```

The `replaced` of each `.reconcile` deletes the manager folder of the program of the command that `replaced` receives, when that command is inside the program folder of a manager (see Program and manager folder) and that manager folder is not the manager folder of the program calling `.reconcile`.
`replaced` deletes that manager folder only while holding the lock of the `instance.lock` of that folder (see The 'single' manager in Implementation notes): when a manager of that folder is running, `replaced` sends `Quit` to that manager and waits for the lock, at most 30 seconds; after that wait, `replaced` deletes every file of that manager folder that can be deleted, and that manager quits (I6).

